# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What the project keeps out of version control.
#
# The rule changed when the project became a multi-unit pipeline. It used to
# publish only the finished website; it now has to be able to rebuild that
# website from scratch, which means the pipeline and the transcriptions travel
# with it. What stays out is bulk that can be re-derived, or that is not ours.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Model output caches. About $29 of API output, and re-derivable by paying
# again, so they are kept on this machine but never published.
/cache/
/retranscription-opus/
/retranscription-sonnet/

# 1.08 GB of archival masters. site/assets/scans/ carries the derivatives.
pages/

# Generated review sheets and reports. Rebuilt by the pipeline on demand;
# the decisions they lead to are recorded in units/<slug>/rulings.yml and
# reference/, which are tracked.
/review/

# Build output
site/_site/
site/.jekyll-cache/
site/.jekyll-metadata
site/vendor/
.bundle/

# Working files and one-offs left at the project root
/*.txt
/*.csv
/final_dates.json
*.bak*
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# API credential
.anthropic_key

